{title: A Brother to the Scum of the Earth}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 99}

Chorus:
[D]We are the salt
[G]We are the [D]light
[D]We are the souls You [A]have made [D]right
With [D]thankful hearts our [G]praise we [D]sing
To [Em]You, our [D/F#]Brother, [G]Friend and [Asus]King![A]

Verse 1:
You [A]love us all
You [D]know our name
How [A]can we ever [D]be the same?
Your [F#m]grace and mercy [Bm]all around
And [G]what was lost has [Asus]now been found.[A]

Verse 2:
[A]To all [A]who hunger, [D]You are Bread
[A]And by Your life our [D]souls are fed
To [F#m]those who thirst, Your Waters flow
[G]Your Word is all we need to [A]know.

Verse 3:
[A]Into our world You came [D]by birth
[A]A Brother to the [D]scum of the earth
And [F#m]for our lives [A]You hung [Bm]in pain
To [G]pay the price, then rise again!
